{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StaircaseHookMultiset","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.StaircaseHookMultiset","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumBetaCoordinates"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hookSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hookSum","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L131-L164","doc":"**The telescoped hook sum of the staircase.**  For any `g` into an additive commutative\nmonoid,\n\n    Σ_{c ∈ δ_k} g(h(c))  =  Σ_{s<k} (s+1) • g(2(k−s) − 1) .\n\nThis is the identity the `REV_n` arc consumes.  Reindexing `s = k − j` turns the right-hand\nside into `Σ_{j=1}^{k} (k+1−j) g(2j−1)`, which at `g = ε` is the staircase's β-side — and with\n`betaSide_eq_hookSum` that is the whole of `V(δ_k)` bar the `L`-free constant.\n\nThe proof is the antidiagonal fibration: the hook is constant on each antidiagonal\n(`staircase_hook`) and antidiagonal `s` has `s+1` cells (`staircaseYD_antidiag_card`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_antidiag_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_antidiag_card","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L125-L129","doc":"Antidiagonal `s` carries exactly `s + 1` cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_filter_antidiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_filter_antidiag","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L112-L123","doc":"The antidiagonal `s` of the staircase: the cells with `i + j = s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hook_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hook_odd","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L105-L110","doc":"Every hook length of the staircase is **odd**, and no even value occurs — immediate from\n`staircase_hook`, and the half of the multiset claim that is easiest to misstate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hook","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L96-L103","doc":"**The staircase's hook length, in closed form.**  On a cell, `h(i, j) = 2(k − i − j) − 1`.\n\nIt depends only on the antidiagonal index `s = i + j`, which is the whole content: the hook is\nconstant along antidiagonals, and antidiagonal `s` carries `s + 1` cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_colLen","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L86-L94","doc":"`colLen j = k − j`, by the same argument — the presentation is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_rowLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD_rowLen","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L76-L84","doc":"`rowLen i = k − i`.  Read off `mem_iff_lt_rowLen`: `j` is in row `i` iff `j < k − i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.mem_staircaseYD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.mem_staircaseYD","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L71-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircaseYD","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/StaircaseHookMultiset.lean#L58-L69","doc":"The staircase `δ_k = (k, k−1, …, 1)` as a Young diagram, presented as the sublevel set\n`{(i, j) : i + j < k}`.  Visibly symmetric in `i` and `j`, which is what makes `colLen` free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}